     "page": 1,
     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Ramos and Sons Medical Group\nPatient: Carla Hammond DOB: 06/20/1968 Sex: F MRN: 488324\n\nEncounters:\n 2025-02-10 URI BP 151/83 Wt 158\n 2023-12-11 Supraventricular tachycardia (SVT) BP 140/79 Wt 162\n 2022-10-10 Supraventricular tachycardia (SVT) BP 147/79 Wt 158\n 2021-08-09 Supraventricular tachycardia (SVT) BP 152/80 Wt 160\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n • Supraventricular tachycardia (SVT) (kind svt; ablated) - controlled; meds: none\n\n---\n\nDear Life Insurer,\n\nThis is to provide a comprehensive clinical summary of Ms. Carla Hammond, a 56-year-old female under my care at Ramos and Sons Medical Group. The enclosed summary includes details of her medical history, recent encounters, assessments, and ongoing plans.\n\n### Patient Background:\nMs. Hammond was diagnosed with Supraventricular Tachycardia (SVT) in March 2020. This condition, a form of supraventricular tachycardia, was effectively managed with an ablation procedure in April 2020. Since then, her SVT has well-controlled, and she has not required any medications for this condition.\n\n### Recent Encounters:\n\n**2025-02-10:** Ms. Hammond presented with symptoms of an upper respiratory infection (URI). Her blood pressure was recorded at 151/83, and she weighed 158 pounds at the time. During the visit, she reported symptoms consistent with a URI, including nasal congestion, sore throat, and mild cough. A physical examination revealed no significant abnormalities other than the upper respiratory symptoms. Vital signs were otherwise stable, and no additional interventions were necessary beyond symptomatic management.\n\n**2023-12-11:** Ms. Hammond returned for a follow-up related to her SVT. Her blood pressure was 140/79, and she weighed 162 pounds. She reported no episodes of tachycardia since her last visit. An electrocardiogram (ECG) and a Holter monitor evaluation revealed no arrhythmic events. Echocardiographic studies performed during this visit indicated normal left ventricular function and no structural heart disease. She continues to be symptom-free and stable.\n\n**2022-10-10:** Ms. Hammond had an appointment to monitor her SVT condition. Her blood pressure was 147/79, and she weighed 158 pounds. She reported feeling well overall with no recent episodes of tachycardia. An ECG was performed, showing no abnormal rhythms. The echocardiogram confirmed the absence of structural heart disease. We advised her to continue with her regular physical activity, which includes running 3-4 times per week, and to report any symptoms immediately.\n\n**2021-08-09:** Ms. Hammond came in for"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "a follow-up regarding her SVT. Her blood pressure was 152/80, and she weighed 160 pounds. She mentioned sporadic palpitations but no full-blown SVT episodes. An ECG was conducted, showing normal sinus rhythm, and a Holter monitor revealed no arrhythmic events. Echocardiographic findings were normal, indicating no structural heart abnormalities. Given her stable condition, we recommended continuing her current management plan.\n\n### Assessment and Plan:\n\n**Supraventricular Tachycardia (SVT):**\n- **Type:** Supraventricular Tachycardia (SVT)\n- **Procedure:** SVT ablation performed in April **Status:** Controlled\n- **Current Medications:** None\n\nMs. Hammond remains under careful surveillance for any signs of SVT recurrence. She reports no symptoms since her ablation, and all diagnostic evaluations to date have shown no evidence of arrhythmic activity or structural heart disease. Her current management includes regular follow-ups every 6-12 months, which she adheres to diligently.\n\n### Additional Health Information:\n\n**Vital Signs:**\n- Blood Pressure: 151/83 on 2025-02-10, 140/79 on 2023-12-11, 147/79 on 2022-10-10, 152/80 on 2021-08-09\n- Weight: 158 pounds on 2025-02-10, 162 pounds on 2023-12-11, 158 pounds on 160 pounds on 2021-08-09\n\n**Exercise:**\nMs. Hammond engages in regular physical activity, running 3-4 times a week, which has been beneficial for her overall cardiovascular health.\n\n**Family History:**\n- **Mother:** \n - Colon cancer, diagnosed at age 45, deceased at age 52\n - COPD, diagnosed at age 76, currently living at age 89\n\nMs. Hammond is a non-smoker and does consume alcohol. There is no documented history of tobacco use.\n\nI hope this summary provides the comprehensive clinical overview needed for your evaluation. Please feel free to contact me if you require any further information.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Amy Myers, MD \nCardiology Specialist \nRamos and Sons Medical Group\n"
